title: Coming from Cucumber.js
section: Introduction
desc: What stays the same and what changes when you move a Cucumber.js suite to bddr: feature files, steps, hooks, world, and running.
lede: Your feature files do not change. The step code changes shape a little: bddr passes a context instead of using this, and hooks have more levels.
---
<h2>What stays the same</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Feature files.</strong> Gherkin, Background, Scenario Outline, Rule, tags, data tables and doc strings work as before. bddr parses with the Cucumber Gherkin parser.</li>
  <li><strong>Step patterns.</strong> Cucumber Expressions and regular expressions, with <code>{int}</code>, <code>{string}</code> and custom parameter types.</li>
  <li><strong>Tag expressions.</strong> <code>-t "@smoke and not @wip"</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>Reports.</strong> Cucumber JSON and Cucumber Messages are available as reporters, next to JUnit XML and HTML.</li>
</ul>

<h2>What changes</h2>
<div class="table-wrap"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Cucumber.js</th><th>bddr</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td><code>this</code> in a step is the World</td><td>The first argument is the context: <code>(ctx, ...args)</code>. Use <code>ctx.state</code> for scenario data.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>setWorldConstructor</code> and a World class</td><td>Fixtures: <code>defineFixture('page', ...)</code>. See <a href="fixtures.html">Fixtures and inject()</a>.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>Before</code>, <code>After</code>, <code>BeforeAll</code>, <code>AfterAll</code></td><td>The same names, plus worker, group, feature, rule and step levels. See <a href="hooks.html">Hooks</a>.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>BeforeStep</code>, <code>AfterStep</code></td><td>The same names.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>defineParameterType</code></td><td>The same name and options: <code>name</code>, <code>regexp</code>, <code>transformer</code>.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>cucumber.js</code> profiles file</td><td><code>bddr.config.ts</code> with <code>profiles</code>. See <a href="configuration.html">Configuration</a>.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>--parallel 4</code></td><td><code>--workers 4</code>, with an optional <code>--pool process</code>.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>--retry 2</code></td><td><code>--retry 2</code>, and also per scenario with <code>@retry:2</code>, per group, and per step.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>--name</code>, <code>--tags</code></td><td>The same, as <code>--name</code> and <code>-t</code>.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Steps in <code>support/</code> loaded with <code>--require</code></td><td>The config's <code>steps</code> glob.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>

<h2>A step, before and after</h2>
<div class="tabs" data-group="cuke">
  <section data-tab="cucumber" data-label="Cucumber.js">
<cb title="steps/login.steps.ts">import { Given, When, Then } from '@cucumber/cucumber';

Given('I am on the login page', async function () {
  await this.page.goto('/login');
});

When('I sign in as {string}', async function (user: string) {
  await this.page.getByLabel('User').fill(user);
  this.lastUser = user;
});</cb>
  </section>
  <section data-tab="bddr" data-label="bddr">
<cb title="steps/login.steps.ts">import { Given, When } from '@bddr/runtime';

Given('I am on the login page', ({ page }) => page.goto('/login'));

When('I sign in as {string}', async ({ page, state }, user: string) => {
  await page.getByLabel('User').fill(user);
  state.set('lastUser', user);
});</cb>
  </section>
</div>
<p>There is no <code>this</code> and no World class. Ask for the fixtures you need in the first parameter. The <code>page</code> fixture comes from the <a href="playwright.html">Playwright plugin</a>.</p>

<h2>Move in four steps</h2>
<ol class="steps">
  <li><h4>Keep the feature files</h4><p>Point <code>features</code> in the config at them. Run <code>npx bddr validate</code> to see what needs attention.</p></li>
  <li><h4>Change the import</h4><p>Replace <code>@cucumber/cucumber</code> with <code>@bddr/runtime</code>. Hooks and <code>defineParameterType</code> keep their names.</p></li>
  <li><h4>Replace <code>this</code></h4><p>Take <code>ctx</code> or destructured fixtures as the first parameter. Move World properties to <code>ctx.state</code> or to fixtures.</p></li>
  <li><h4>Add the plugin for your browser or API library</h4><p>See <a href="playwright.html">Playwright</a>, <a href="selenium.html">Selenium</a> and <a href="axios.html">axios</a>.</p></li></ol>
<aside class="callout note"><p class="callout-title">No codemod yet</p><p>A tool that rewrites <code>this</code> into context calls is on the list but does not exist. Plan to edit step files by hand. Arrow functions work in bddr, which makes the edit mostly mechanical.</p></aside>

<h2>What you gain</h2>
<p>Groups, dependencies, locks, serial features, retries and quarantine, sharding and the process pool. See <a href="why-bddr.html">Why bddr</a>.</p>
